{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba profiles/manager.md | sed -n '1086,1170p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1086\t\n  1087\t1. first and unique `tree <full-lowercase-id>`, without continuation;\n  1088\t2. contiguous zero-or-more `parent <full-lowercase-id>` records, without\n  1089\t   continuation and retaining byte order;\n  1090\t3. exactly one non-empty `author` and then exactly one non-empty `committer`,\n  1091\t   without continuation; and\n  1092\t4. zero-or-more extra headers whose keys are not `tree`, `parent`, `author`,\n  1093\t   or `committer`, followed by the exact separator.\n  1094\t\n  1095\tAn annotated tag has exactly this order:\n  1096\t\n  1097\t1. first and unique `object <full-lowercase-id>`;\n  1098\t2. unique `type commit` or `type tag`;\n  1099\t3. unique `tag <safe-tag-name>` using section 11.2's byte grammar;\n  1100\t4. OPTIONAL one non-empty `tagger`; and\n  1101\t5. zero-or-more extra headers whose keys are not `object`, `type`, `tag`, or\n  1102\t   `tagger`, followed by the exact separator.\n  1103\t\n  1104\tRequired tag headers admit no continuation. When an exact declared tag ref\n  1105\tselects an annotated chain, the outermost annotated tag object's `tag` value\n  1106\tMUST byte-equal the requested tag; nested tag names need only pass the safe-tag\n  1107\tgrammar. After recomputation, each target's actual type MUST byte-equal the\n  1108\tdeclared `type`. `tag` continues peeling and `commit` terminates it; tree/blob\n  1109\ttargets are invalid. A lightweight tag points directly to a commit and uses no\n  1110\tannotated-depth slot. A chain has at most 16 annotated tag objects and no\n  1111\trepeated full object ID.\n  1112\t\n  1113\tDuplicate, misplaced, malformed, wrong-width, wrong-case, wrong-type, cyclic,\n  1114\tover-depth, outer-tag-name-mismatch, or missing-separator commit/tag data fails\n  1115\t`build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid`.\n  1116\t\n  1117\tThe terminal commit selects exactly one tree. A tree is fully consumed as\n  1118\t`<octal-mode> SP <name> NUL <binary-object-id>`. Names are non-empty portable\n  1119\tUTF-8 components with no slash, NUL, dot component, duplicate, or platform\n  1120\tcollision. Only tree mode `40000` and blob modes `100644` and `100755` are\n  1121\taccepted. Symlink `120000`, gitlink `160000`, special/unknown modes, and\n  1122\tmode/type mismatch fail before snapshot materialization. The manager proves\n  1123\tevery reachable tree/blob locally available and materializes only exact\n  1124\tverified blob bytes as regular files, preserving only the executable-bit\n  1125\tdistinction.\n  1126\t\n  1127\tEvery reachable blob is scanned once before materialization, regardless of\n  1128\tpath, mode, extension, descriptor target, or selected build root. A non-empty\n  1129\tblob below 1024 bytes is rejected when it matches the accepted decoder/encoder\n  1130\tfamily in Git LFS 3.7.1 `lfs/pointer.go`. The compatibility parser:\n  1131\t\n  1132\t1. trims only the Go 1.25 `unicode.IsSpace` UTF-8 encodings from both ends;\n  1133\t2. splits on LF, removes one terminal CR per line, and ignores empty lines;\n  1134\t3. splits each non-empty line at its first ASCII space;\n  1135\t4. accepts required keys exactly once in state order `version`, `oid`, `size`,\n  1136\t   with extension lines allowed before any still-pending required key and no\n  1137\t   line after `size`;\n  1138\t5. accepts exactly the current version\n  1139\t   `https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1` and aliases\n  1140\t   `https://hawser.github.com/spec/v1` and `http://git-media.io/v/2`;\n  1141\t6. requires `oid` to be `sha256:` plus 64 lowercase hexadecimal bytes;\n  1142\t7. parses `size` exactly as Go base-10 signed-int64 input and requires a\n  1143\t   nonnegative value, so `+1`, `00`, and `01` are accepted;\n  1144\t8. accepts an extension key beginning `ext-`, one ASCII digit, `-`, and one\n  1145\t   or more ASCII word bytes, while retaining later non-space/non-LF suffix\n  1146\t   bytes as part of the raw name; its value uses the exact OID grammar;\n  1147\t9. applies last-value-wins to an identical raw extension key and rejects\n  1148\t   distinct surviving extension keys with the same numeric priority; and\n  1149\t10. rejects the pointer match on a missing/unknown required key, malformed\n  1150\t    value, bad extension, or duplicate priority.\n  1151\t\n  1152\tExact canonical and legacy/noncanonical matches both fail\n  1153\t`build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported`. Zero bytes and 1024 bytes or more are\n  1154\toutside that detector. Unknown versions, malformed, uppercase, or wrong-width\n  1155\tOIDs,\n  1156\tmissing required keys, invalid extensions, or distinct duplicate extension\n  1157\tpriorities are ordinary blob bytes, not hydration instructions. The manager\n  1158\tMUST NOT invoke Git LFS, a filter, an LFS endpoint, or `.git/lfs`.\n  1159\t\n  1160\t### 11.6 Snapshot, audit, and cache ordering\n  1161\t\n  1162\tFor every active external repository, the manager:\n  1163\t\n  1164\t1. completes exact source acquisition and, for a declared tag, exact tag\n  1165\t   equality with the immutable lock;\n  1166\t2. proves the complete object graph and LFS absence;\n  1167\t3. freezes and validates the complete regular-file repository snapshot;\n  1168\t4. computes `curator-build-source-v1` over every file, including\n  1169\t   `curator-build.json` and files outside the selected build root;\n  1170\t5. parses the descriptor and validates the selected target/module containment;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
