{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"task-board resource get TASK-260720-1nvomm TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md --output - | nl -ba | sed -n '285,460p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"task-board resource get TASK-260720-1nvomm TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md --output - | nl -ba | sed -n '285,460p'\"","aggregated_output":"   285\t### 6.1 Trusted distribution, process graph, and clean environment\n   286\t\n   287\tThe manager resolves an operator-trusted Git distribution before reading a\n   288\tpackage or substitution path. The absolute `git` executable, its complete\n   289\t`GIT_EXEC_PATH`, HTTPS helper, and every Git subprogram that the fixed fetch can\n   290\tstart MUST be bundled, fingerprinted, or pinned by trusted operator policy. The\n   291\tselected release family MUST be one tested against the driver vectors and MUST\n   292\tsupport `--object-format`, `--ref-format=files`, `--no-lazy-fetch`,\n   293\t`--no-write-fetch-head`, and `--no-auto-maintenance`. A newer or older unknown\n   294\tfamily is rejected, not approximated.\n   295\t\n   296\tThe permitted child graph is exactly:\n   297\t\n   298\t- manager -> absolute trusted `git` for manager-owned `init` and `fetch`;\n   299\t- manager -> the same absolute trusted `git` for one manager-owned, read-only\n   300\t  `cat-file --batch` session after network acquisition or inert local-store\n   301\t  copying;\n   302\t- `git fetch` -> regular executables below the fingerprinted `GIT_EXEC_PATH`\n   303\t  that the selected Git family uses for fetch/pack ingestion;\n   304\t- HTTPS only: the fingerprinted `git-remote-https` and an optional\n   305\t  manager-owned credential broker;\n   306\t- SSH only: a manager-owned binary SSH wrapper and one operator-trusted\n   307\t  OpenSSH executable;\n   308\t- no shell, arbitrary remote helper, local/source upload-pack, maintenance,\n   309\t  submodule child, checkout filter, hook, LFS client, pager, editor, proxy\n   310\t  command, package program, or produced artifact.\n   311\t\n   312\tThe `cat-file` child MUST NOT start another process. An observed local child\n   313\toutside that graph is a conformance failure. The\n   314\tpackage/descriptor can select only a validated HTTPS or SSH source spelling; it\n   315\tcannot select the Git binary, exec path, helper, upload-pack, credential\n   316\tbroker, SSH client, object-reader arguments, or child arguments.\n   317\t\n   318\tEvery Git child uses a manager-owned empty CWD and an environment constructed\n   319\tfrom empty. It contains only indispensable OS process variables, private\n   320\thome/config/temp paths, normalized locale, the fingerprinted exec path, and:\n   321\t\n   322\t```text\n   323\tGIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=<manager-owned zero-byte regular file>\n   324\tGIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=<manager-owned zero-byte regular file>\n   325\tGIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1\n   326\tGIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1\n   327\tGIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1\n   328\tGIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0\n   329\tGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0\n   330\tGIT_PAGER=cat\n   331\tGIT_PROTOCOL_FROM_USER=0\n   332\tGIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS=1\n   333\tGIT_ATTR_NOSYSTEM=1\n   334\tGIT_EXEC_PATH=<fingerprinted trusted Git exec path>\n   335\tHOME=<operation-private>/home\n   336\tXDG_CONFIG_HOME=<operation-private>/config\n   337\tLC_ALL=C\n   338\tLANG=C\n   339\t```\n   340\t\n   341\tFor SSH it additionally sets only\n   342\t`GIT_SSH=<absolute-manager-wrapper>`, `GIT_SSH_VARIANT=ssh`, and the\n   343\tmanager-private policy-FD number. `GIT_PROTOCOL` is absent and the fixed\n   344\tconfiguration uses protocol version 0, so Git MUST NOT add an SSH\n   345\t`SendEnv=GIT_PROTOCOL` option. For HTTPS, `GIT_ASKPASS` names either the\n   346\tmanager credential broker or a fail-closed manager broker.\n   347\t\n   348\tThe manager unsets `GIT_DIR`, `GIT_WORK_TREE`, `GIT_COMMON_DIR`,\n   349\t`GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY`, `GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES`, `GIT_NAMESPACE`,\n   350\t`GIT_REPLACE_REF_BASE`, `GIT_ATTR_SOURCE`, `GIT_SSL_NO_VERIFY`,\n   351\t`GIT_SSH_COMMAND`, `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, `SSH_ASKPASS`, `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`,\n   352\t`GIT_CONFIG_KEY_*`, `GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_*`, all trace variables, all HTTP/HTTPS\n   353\tproxy variables, and every other inherited `GIT_*`/`SSH_*` variable. `PATH` is\n   354\ta manager-owned empty directory except for exact helper basenames that the\n   355\tfingerprinted Git family cannot launch by absolute exec-path resolution.\n   356\t\n   357\tHTTPS verifies TLS and does not follow redirects. An operator proxy or\n   358\tcredential may be supplied only through manager policy/broker state, never the\n   359\tmanifest, descriptor, source repository, or compiler environment.\n   360\t\n   361\t### 6.2 Exact private repository initialization\n   362\t\n   363\tBefore each network attempt the manager exclusively creates a new empty\n   364\toperation-private directory, an actual zero-entry template directory, empty\n   365\thooks directory, and private bare-repository path. It invokes exactly:\n   366\t\n   367\t```json\n   368\t[\n   369\t  \"<absolute-trusted-git>\",\n   370\t  \"--git-dir=<operation-private>/repo.git\",\n   371\t  \"-c\",\n   372\t  \"init.defaultBranch=curator-invalid\",\n   373\t  \"init\",\n   374\t  \"--bare\",\n   375\t  \"--quiet\",\n   376\t  \"--template=<operation-private>/empty-template\",\n   377\t  \"--object-format=<sha1-or-sha256>\",\n   378\t  \"--ref-format=files\"\n   379\t]\n   380\t```\n   381\t\n   382\tThere is no repository path operand, global/user/system template, initial\n   383\tbranch from configuration, shared mode, separate Git directory, worktree, or\n   384\tsource-provided config. After exit, manager code opens the result with\n   385\tno-follow/rooted access and requires:\n   386\t\n   387\t- one ordinary bare repository inside operation-private state;\n   388\t- `core.repositoryformatversion`/`extensions.objectFormat` consistent with the\n   389\t  requested object format and files refs;\n   390\t- no remote, alternate, promisor, partial-clone, worktree, replace, graft,\n   391\t  shallow, hook, filter, or unknown extension state;\n   392\t- no link, reparse escape, special file, unexpected owner/ACL, or writable\n   393\t  boundary outside the operation principal.\n   394\t\n   395\tFailure discards the directory. The manager never repairs or adopts it.\n   396\t\n   397\t### 6.3 Exact network fetch and ref flows\n   398\t\n   399\tAll fetches use a direct validated URL, a fresh private repository, one\n   400\tmanager-chosen destination under `refs/curator/`, and this exact common shape:\n   401\t\n   402\t```json\n   403\t[\n   404\t  \"<absolute-trusted-git>\",\n   405\t  \"--git-dir=<operation-private>/repo.git\",\n   406\t  \"--no-replace-objects\",\n   407\t  \"--no-lazy-fetch\",\n   408\t  \"--no-optional-locks\",\n   409\t  \"-c\",\n   410\t  \"protocol.allow=never\",\n   411\t  \"-c\",\n   412\t  \"protocol.<https-or-ssh>.allow=always\",\n   413\t  \"-c\",\n   414\t  \"protocol.version=0\",\n   415\t  \"-c\",\n   416\t  \"credential.helper=\",\n   417\t  \"-c\",\n   418\t  \"core.askPass=<manager-broker>\",\n   419\t  \"-c\",\n   420\t  \"core.hooksPath=<operation-private>/empty-hooks\",\n   421\t  \"-c\",\n   422\t  \"core.fsmonitor=false\",\n   423\t  \"-c\",\n   424\t  \"core.untrackedCache=false\",\n   425\t  \"-c\",\n   426\t  \"submodule.recurse=false\",\n   427\t  \"-c\",\n   428\t  \"fetch.recurseSubmodules=false\",\n   429\t  \"-c\",\n   430\t  \"maintenance.auto=false\",\n   431\t  \"-c\",\n   432\t  \"fetch.writeCommitGraph=false\",\n   433\t  \"-c\",\n   434\t  \"fetch.fsckObjects=true\",\n   435\t  \"-c\",\n   436\t  \"transfer.fsckObjects=true\",\n   437\t  \"-c\",\n   438\t  \"http.followRedirects=false\",\n   439\t  \"-c\",\n   440\t  \"http.sslVerify=true\",\n   441\t  \"-c\",\n   442\t  \"http.proxy=\",\n   443\t  \"-c\",\n   444\t  \"https.proxy=\",\n   445\t  \"fetch\",\n   446\t  \"--quiet\",\n   447\t  \"--atomic\",\n   448\t  \"--no-tags\",\n   449\t  \"--no-recurse-submodules\",\n   450\t  \"--no-auto-maintenance\",\n   451\t  \"--no-write-fetch-head\",\n   452\t  \"--no-write-commit-graph\",\n   453\t  \"--refmap=\",\n   454\t  \"--jobs=1\",\n   455\t  \"--upload-pack=git-upload-pack\",\n   456\t  \"--\",\n   457\t  \"<validated-url>\",\n   458\t  \"<one-manager-refspec>\"\n   459\t]\n   460\t```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
