{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"task-board resource get TASK-260720-1nvomm TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md --output - | nl -ba | sed -n '461,620p'\"","aggregated_output":"   461\t\n   462\tThe selected transport is the only `protocol.*.allow=always` entry; the other\n   463\ttransport and every remote-helper protocol remain denied. There is no\n   464\t`--filter`, `--server-option`, remote name, configured refspec, stdin refspec,\n   465\tprune, mirror, depth/shallow option, tag auto-follow, or package-selected\n   466\targument. Top-level `git fetch` receives closed stdin and bounded captured\n   467\tdiagnostics.\n   468\t\n   469\tThe one refspec is selected as follows:\n   470\t\n   471\t1. **Unsubstituted declaration without `tag`:**\n   472\t   Fetch `<full-locked-oid>:refs/curator/locked`. A full hexadecimal object\n   473\t   name is the only non-ref source admitted. On success, manager code still\n   474\t   parses and recomputes that object and requires a commit. A nonzero fetch is\n   475\t   `build_repository_source_unavailable`. There is no tag, branch, advertised\n   476\t   ref, or all-refs fallback.\n   477\t2. **Unsubstituted declaration with `tag`:**\n   478\t   Always fetch\n   479\t   `refs/tags/<tag>:refs/curator/tag` as the sole acquisition attempt. The\n   480\t   manager MUST NOT first or later fetch `<full-locked-oid>`, even when the\n   481\t   server permits direct object-ID wants. Manager code requires exactly the\n   482\t   fixed destination ref, parses and recomputes a lightweight or annotated-tag\n   483\t   chain with section 6.6.2's common grammar, and requires the terminal object\n   484\t   to be a commit exactly equal to `locked_commit.hex`. A different terminal\n   485\t   commit is `build_repository_ref_moved`. A missing exact ref, nonzero fetch,\n   486\t   or transport failure is `build_repository_source_unavailable`. A malformed\n   487\t   or incomplete fetched object graph retains the section 6.6 stable semantic\n   488\t   or incomplete-source error. There is no direct-object, branch, all-tags, or\n   489\t   alternate-ref fallback.\n   490\t3. **Operator network substitution:**  \n   491\t   A full `revision` fetches\n   492\t   `<full-oid>:refs/curator/effective`; a `tag` fetches\n   493\t   `refs/tags/<tag>:refs/curator/effective`; a `branch` fetches\n   494\t   `refs/heads/<branch>:refs/curator/effective`. There is no fallback between\n   495\t   forms. The declared repository lock's object format initializes the private\n   496\t   repository and MUST match the substituted remote; the manager never retries\n   497\t   under another hash family. The exact resulting commit becomes the effective\n   498\t   receipt identity.\n   499\t\n   500\tEvery destination is fixed manager namespace text; remote data cannot choose a\n   501\tlocal ref, refmap, refspec, helper, upload-pack, filter, or server option.\n   502\t`FETCH_HEAD`, remote-tracking refs, local heads/tags, commit-graphs, and\n   503\tmaintenance state MUST remain absent. A nonzero fetch, unexpected local ref,\n   504\tunexpected child, or any write outside the private repository fails and\n   505\tdiscards the attempt.\n   506\t\n   507\tFor an unsubstituted tagged source, exact-tag fetch and terminal-lock equality\n   508\tare preconditions of source resolution. They run before source audit can\n   509\tsucceed, before artifact-cache lookup, and before any compiler child. A failure\n   510\tpublishes no snapshot, audit success, receipt, marker, or artifact. A\n   511\tsyntax-only offline check that cannot perform the exact-tag fetch emits only\n   512\t`build_repository_unverified_offline`; install, update, repair, and\n   513\tcoverage-claiming audit return `build_repository_source_unavailable` before\n   514\tmutation.\n   515\t\n   516\tThe conformance matrix is invariant to direct object-ID want policy because a\n   517\ttagged declaration never issues such a want:\n   518\t\n   519\t```json\n   520\t[\n   521\t  {\n   522\t    \"name\": \"tag-match-direct-oid-wants-denied\",\n   523\t    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"deny\",\n   524\t    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n   525\t    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n   526\t    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n   527\t    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n   528\t    \"result\": \"source-resolved\"\n   529\t  },\n   530\t  {\n   531\t    \"name\": \"tag-moved-direct-oid-wants-denied\",\n   532\t    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"deny\",\n   533\t    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n   534\t    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n   535\t    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"89abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\",\n   536\t    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n   537\t    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_ref_moved\",\n   538\t    \"audit_started\": false,\n   539\t    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n   540\t    \"compiler_started\": false\n   541\t  },\n   542\t  {\n   543\t    \"name\": \"tag-missing-direct-oid-wants-denied\",\n   544\t    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"deny\",\n   545\t    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n   546\t    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n   547\t    \"remote_ref_present\": false,\n   548\t    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_source_unavailable\",\n   549\t    \"audit_started\": false,\n   550\t    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n   551\t    \"compiler_started\": false\n   552\t  },\n   553\t  {\n   554\t    \"name\": \"tag-match-direct-oid-wants-permitted\",\n   555\t    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"permit\",\n   556\t    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n   557\t    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n   558\t    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n   559\t    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n   560\t    \"result\": \"source-resolved\"\n   561\t  },\n   562\t  {\n   563\t    \"name\": \"tag-moved-direct-oid-wants-permitted\",\n   564\t    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"permit\",\n   565\t    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n   566\t    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n   567\t    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"89abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\",\n   568\t    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n   569\t    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_ref_moved\",\n   570\t    \"audit_started\": false,\n   571\t    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n   572\t    \"compiler_started\": false\n   573\t  },\n   574\t  {\n   575\t    \"name\": \"tag-missing-direct-oid-wants-permitted\",\n   576\t    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"permit\",\n   577\t    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n   578\t    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n   579\t    \"remote_ref_present\": false,\n   580\t    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_source_unavailable\",\n   581\t    \"audit_started\": false,\n   582\t    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n   583\t    \"compiler_started\": false\n   584\t  }\n   585\t]\n   586\t```\n   587\t\n   588\t### 6.4 Exact SSH wrapper and OpenSSH invocation\n   589\t\n   590\tSSH sources retain the section-3 canonical identity but are further narrowed\n   591\tfor this driver: the raw repository path supplied to the remote shell MUST use\n   592\tonly ASCII letters, digits, `.`, `_`, `-`, and `/`, with the existing\n   593\tnon-empty/no-`.`/no-`..` component rules. A quote, shell metacharacter,\n   594\twhitespace, escape, or non-ASCII byte is therefore rejected for SSH before\n   595\tGit. HTTPS retains the section-3 path grammar.\n   596\t\n   597\tBefore fetch, the manager creates a protected read-only policy record and\n   598\tpasses an already-open descriptor number to the binary wrapper. The record\n   599\tcontains exactly:\n   600\t\n   601\t- the expected Git destination, either `host` or `user@host`;\n   602\t- the expected raw remote path from the validated SSH URI/SCP spelling;\n   603\t- the expected remote command\n   604\t  `git-upload-pack '<raw-path>'`;\n   605\t- absolute operator-trusted SSH executable, empty SSH config, empty global\n   606\t  known-hosts file, selected operator known-hosts file, timeout, and exactly\n   607\t  one authentication mode.\n   608\t\n   609\tBecause the allowed path alphabet excludes `'`, the command has no escaping\n   610\tbranch. The wrapper does not accept a policy pathname from argv/environment and\n   611\tdoes not consult package/project files.\n   612\t\n   613\t`GIT_SSH_VARIANT=ssh` suppresses variant autodetection. With fixed Git protocol\n   614\t0 and no port/IP-family option, the wrapper accepts exactly:\n   615\t\n   616\t```text\n   617\targv[0] = <absolute-manager-wrapper>\n   618\targv[1] = <expected host or user@host>\n   619\targv[2] = <exact expected git-upload-pack command>\n   620\targc    = 3\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
