{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"task-board resource get TASK-260720-1nvomm TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md --output - | nl -ba | sed -n '621,820p'\"","aggregated_output":"   621\t```\n   622\t\n   623\tIt rejects `-G`, `-p`, `-4`, `-6`, `-o`, `SendEnv`, extra operands, a different\n   624\thost/user/path/upload-pack, and every other shape. A tested Git family whose\n   625\tactual wrapper call differs is unsupported until a new reviewed wrapper\n   626\trevision is defined.\n   627\t\n   628\tAfter byte-exact comparison, the wrapper directly executes the\n   629\toperator-trusted SSH binary without a shell. The common argv is exactly:\n   630\t\n   631\t```json\n   632\t[\n   633\t  \"<absolute-operator-trusted-ssh>\",\n   634\t  \"-F\",\n   635\t  \"<manager-owned-empty-ssh-config>\",\n   636\t  \"-T\",\n   637\t  \"-o\",\n   638\t  \"BatchMode=yes\",\n   639\t  \"-o\",\n   640\t  \"NumberOfPasswordPrompts=0\",\n   641\t  \"-o\",\n   642\t  \"PasswordAuthentication=no\",\n   643\t  \"-o\",\n   644\t  \"KbdInteractiveAuthentication=no\",\n   645\t  \"-o\",\n   646\t  \"PreferredAuthentications=publickey\",\n   647\t  \"-o\",\n   648\t  \"HostbasedAuthentication=no\",\n   649\t  \"-o\",\n   650\t  \"GSSAPIAuthentication=no\",\n   651\t  \"-o\",\n   652\t  \"StrictHostKeyChecking=yes\",\n   653\t  \"-o\",\n   654\t  \"UserKnownHostsFile=<operator-known-hosts>\",\n   655\t  \"-o\",\n   656\t  \"GlobalKnownHostsFile=<manager-owned-empty-known-hosts>\",\n   657\t  \"-o\",\n   658\t  \"CheckHostIP=no\",\n   659\t  \"-o\",\n   660\t  \"VerifyHostKeyDNS=no\",\n   661\t  \"-o\",\n   662\t  \"UpdateHostKeys=no\",\n   663\t  \"-o\",\n   664\t  \"ForwardAgent=no\",\n   665\t  \"-o\",\n   666\t  \"ForwardX11=no\",\n   667\t  \"-o\",\n   668\t  \"ClearAllForwardings=yes\",\n   669\t  \"-o\",\n   670\t  \"PermitLocalCommand=no\",\n   671\t  \"-o\",\n   672\t  \"ProxyCommand=none\",\n   673\t  \"-o\",\n   674\t  \"ProxyJump=none\",\n   675\t  \"-o\",\n   676\t  \"ControlMaster=no\",\n   677\t  \"-o\",\n   678\t  \"ControlPath=none\",\n   679\t  \"-o\",\n   680\t  \"ControlPersist=no\",\n   681\t  \"-o\",\n   682\t  \"RequestTTY=no\",\n   683\t  \"-o\",\n   684\t  \"EscapeChar=none\",\n   685\t  \"-o\",\n   686\t  \"EnableEscapeCommandline=no\",\n   687\t  \"-o\",\n   688\t  \"CanonicalizeHostname=no\",\n   689\t  \"-o\",\n   690\t  \"ConnectionAttempts=1\",\n   691\t  \"-o\",\n   692\t  \"ConnectTimeout=<manager-policy-seconds>\",\n   693\t  \"<one-authentication-tail>\",\n   694\t  \"<expected host or user@host>\",\n   695\t  \"<exact expected git-upload-pack command>\"\n   696\t]\n   697\t```\n   698\t\n   699\tThe authentication tail is exactly one of:\n   700\t\n   701\t```text\n   702\toperator identity file:\n   703\t  -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -o IdentityAgent=none -i <operator-selected-identity>\n   704\t\n   705\toperator SSH agent:\n   706\t  -o IdentitiesOnly=no -o IdentityFile=none\n   707\t  -o IdentityAgent=<operator-selected-agent-socket>\n   708\t```\n   709\t\n   710\tThe private `HOME` contains no default identity files. Package data cannot\n   711\tselect the identity, agent, known-hosts, timeout, SSH config, host-key policy,\n   712\tor option. The wrapper passes no ambient `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`.\n   713\t\n   714\tThe top-level fetch has no inherited terminal stdin. SSH standard input/output\n   715\tare necessarily the private Git-upload-pack protocol pipes created by trusted\n   716\tGit; they are not a TTY, user input, package file, or prompt channel. The\n   717\twrapper neither parses nor replaces that protocol stream. This is the only\n   718\tstdin carried through SSH; closing it would make Git transport impossible.\n   719\t\n   720\t### 6.5 Local substitution admission: deliberately narrow v1\n   721\t\n   722\tLocal substitutions execute no Git command, upload-pack, hook, filter, helper,\n   723\tor LFS process from the source repository. Manager code treats repository\n   724\tadministration files and object stores as untrusted data.\n   725\t\n   726\tV1 admits only an ordinary non-bare worktree whose substitution root is a\n   727\tlink-free directory and whose `.git` entry is a link-free directory directly\n   728\tbelow that root. Stable pre-audit rejections are:\n   729\t\n   730\t- `.git` is a regular gitfile: `build_repository_local_gitfile_unsupported`;\n   731\t- `.git` is absent and the selected path is a bare repository:\n   732\t  `build_repository_local_bare_unsupported`;\n   733\t- `.git/commondir`, `.git/worktrees`, or `.git/config.worktree` exists:\n   734\t  `build_repository_local_linked_worktree_unsupported`;\n   735\t- `.git` or any admitted administration/object component is a link, reparse\n   736\t  point, special file, multiply linked mutable file, or containment escape:\n   737\t  `build_repository_local_layout_unsafe`.\n   738\t\n   739\tThe manager never follows or opens a gitfile/commondir target in v1. This makes\n   740\ttheir containment rule exact: no path outside `<substitution-root>/.git` is\n   741\tadmitted. Supporting ordinary gitfiles, linked worktrees, submodule worktrees,\n   742\tor bare repositories requires a new admission algorithm and conformance\n   743\tvectors, not a fallback to Git discovery.\n   744\t\n   745\t#### 6.5.1 Byte-level config admission\n   746\t\n   747\tThe manager opens `.git/config` no-follow as a bounded regular file and parses\n   748\tthis data-only subset:\n   749\t\n   750\t1. bytes are valid UTF-8 with LF or CRLF records, optional final line ending,\n   751\t   and no BOM, NUL, lone CR, control byte other than tab in a value, or\n   752\t   backslash line continuation;\n   753\t2. section names and variable names are ASCII case-insensitive\n   754\t   `[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9-]*` tokens; subsections are double-quoted UTF-8 with\n   755\t   only `\\\\` and `\\\"` escapes;\n   756\t3. values are one-line unquoted text or one double-quoted value with only\n   757\t   `\\\\`, `\\\"`, `\\n`, `\\t`, and `\\b` escapes; comment markers are recognized\n   758\t   only outside quotes; malformed/unsupported syntax rejects the repository;\n   759\t4. `[include]` and `[includeIf \"...\"]` are rejected before resolving a path;\n   760\t5. duplicate security-relevant keys reject even when values match.\n   761\t\n   762\tOther well-formed non-extension keys are inert: the manager records but never\n   763\tapplies them. Admission reads only:\n   764\t\n   765\t- `core.repositoryformatversion`, required as integer `0` or `1`;\n   766\t- `core.bare`, required `false`;\n   767\t- `extensions.*`;\n   768\t- every `remote \"<name>\".promisor` and\n   769\t  `remote \"<name>\".partialCloneFilter`.\n   770\t\n   771\tAllowed format states are exactly:\n   772\t\n   773\t- SHA-1: repository format `0`, no `extensions.*`;\n   774\t- SHA-256: repository format `1`, exactly\n   775\t  `extensions.objectFormat=sha256`, with optional\n   776\t  `extensions.refStorage=files`.\n   777\t\n   778\tBoolean values are accepted only as case-insensitive `true`/`yes`/`on`/`1` or\n   779\t`false`/`no`/`off`/`0`; an absent value means true as in Git config.\n   780\t\n   781\t`extensions.refStorage=reftable`, `extensions.partialClone`,\n   782\t`extensions.worktreeConfig`, `extensions.compatObjectFormat`, `noop`,\n   783\t`preciousObjects`, every unknown extension, a true promisor value, or a\n   784\tnon-empty partial-clone filter fails\n   785\t`build_repository_local_format_unsupported`. Reftable is deliberately rejected;\n   786\tdummy `HEAD`/`refs` files are never mistaken for the files backend.\n   787\t\n   788\t#### 6.5.2 Files-ref parsing and selected HEAD\n   789\t\n   790\t`HEAD`, every loose ref below `.git/refs`, and optional `.git/packed-refs` are\n   791\tbounded, link-free regular files. The parser:\n   792\t\n   793\t- accepts `HEAD` as either one full lowercase object ID or\n   794\t  `ref: refs/heads/<safe-name>` plus exactly one LF/CRLF or EOF;\n   795\t- permits only one level of HEAD symbolic reference; the selected loose/packed\n   796\t  head itself contains one full lowercase object ID, never another symref;\n   797\t- validates every ref name with the section-3 safe ref grammar and the\n   798\t  protocol-defined equivalent of `git check-ref-format`;\n   799\t- parses `packed-refs` as an optional `# pack-refs with:` header whose unique\n   800\t  space-separated traits are drawn only from `peeled`, `fully-peeled`, and\n   801\t  `sorted`, then\n   802\t  `<full-oid> SP <refname>` records and optional `^<full-oid>` peeled records\n   803\t  only immediately after a tag record; it rejects duplicates, unsupported\n   804\t  headers, wrong hash lengths/case, malformed lines, and ref/peeled conflicts;\n   805\t- rejects any loose or packed `refs/replace/*` entry, regardless of whether it\n   806\t  is reachable or selected.\n   807\t\n   808\tLoose refs have Git's normal precedence over packed refs, but contradictory\n   809\tduplicate loose files and platform-colliding ref paths reject rather than\n   810\tchoose. The selected HEAD object ID is the effective commit recorded in the\n   811\treceipt. Dirty index/worktree/untracked bytes are never opened as source.\n   812\t\n   813\t#### 6.5.3 Exact object inventory and interoperable pack admission\n   814\t\n   815\tBefore interpreting an object, the manager freezes one inventory generation and\n   816\tcopies the allowed bytes into operation-private inert holding state. It\n   817\tre-stats and rehashes every admitted source file after copy; any addition,\n   818\tremoval, rename, metadata identity change, or byte change aborts.\n   819\t\n   820\tAllowed object-store entries are exactly:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
