{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba cli/curator.md | sed -n '1,105p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Curator CLI guide\n     2\t\n     3\tThis document is informative. It describes the Go reference implementation,\n     4\tnot a conformance requirement. Other managers may use different command names,\n     5\tflags, output, machine-home paths, and distribution channels.\n     6\t\n     7\tCurator uses `curator`, defaults its machine home to `~/.curator`, reads user\n     8\tconfiguration from `~/.curator/config.json`, and supports overrides through\n     9\t`CURATOR_CONFIG` and `CURATOR_SYSTEM_CONFIG`. Those names are not protocol wire\n    10\tidentifiers.\n    11\t\n    12\t## Commands\n    13\t\n    14\t| Command | Behavior |\n    15\t|---|---|\n    16\t| `curator bootstrap [--if-missing]` | Create machine configuration interactively or from flags; keep an existing file unchanged with `--if-missing` |\n    17\t| `curator init [path]` | Create `Skillfile.json` and ignore generated paths |\n    18\t| `curator add <name> --tag\\|--branch\\|--revision <ref>` | Add or replace a direct declaration and install |\n    19\t| `curator remove <name>` | Remove a declaration |\n    20\t| `curator install [target] [--all] [--dry-run] [--strict-tags] [--audit [advisory\\|strict]]` | Apply the manager lifecycle |\n    21\t| `curator update` | Fetch configured source repositories |\n    22\t| `curator upgrade [target] [--all] [--dry-run]` | Fetch only the selected dependency closure, then install |\n    23\t| `curator status [target] [--all] [--check] [--json] [--attest]` | Report drift and optionally refresh attestations |\n    24\t| `curator list` | List configured projects and declarations |\n    25\t| `curator project add\\|resolve` | Register projects and resolve ownership of a path |\n    26\t| `curator config show` | Print effective configuration |\n    27\t| `curator skill check <dir> [--locale <code>] [--json]` | Validate one package |\n    28\t| `curator global init\\|add\\|remove\\|list\\|status\\|install\\|update\\|upgrade` | Manage global scope |\n    29\t| `curator hybrid add\\|remove\\|list\\|status` | Manage hybrid scope |\n    30\t| `curator audit [target] [--all] [--global] [--json]` | Run source audit |\n    31\t| `curator audit --allow <hash> --reason <text>` | Create an operator pin |\n    32\t| `curator audit --publish <record> --registry <url>` | Publish an auditor-signed record |\n    33\t| `curator repair [target] [--all] [--audit [advisory\\|strict]]` | rc.5 command contract: reacquire, audit, and restore non-current managed state |\n    34\t| `curator gc` | Collect unreferenced machine state |\n    35\t| `curator shell-init [auto\\|zsh\\|bash\\|powershell] [--install] [--no-global]` | Print or cache optional shell integration |\n    36\t\n    37\tExit code 0 is success, including a syntax-only check that emitted only\n    38\twarnings. Exit code 1 is an operation failure, security-policy block, partial\n    39\tmulti-target failure, or `status --check` result containing any non-current or\n    40\tunknown item. Exit code 2 is invalid command syntax or flag use. Scripts should\n    41\tuse `--json` where available and inspect each result's stable `code` rather\n    42\tthan parse human text.\n    43\t\n    44\t`bootstrap --if-missing` is intended for repository bootstrap commands. It\n    45\treturns success without parsing or rewriting an existing configuration and is\n    46\tmutually exclusive with `--force`.\n    47\t\n    48\t`upgrade` differs from `update`: upgrade fetches only direct and transitive\n    49\tsources required by the selected project or global manifest, while update\n    50\tfetches every repository below `skills_root`. `upgrade --all` deduplicates\n    51\trepositories shared by project closures. Any install or upgrade `--dry-run`\n    52\tuses temporary planning state and leaves source checkouts, caches,\n    53\tconfiguration, runtime state, and project artifacts unchanged.\n    54\t\n    55\t## Developer shell\n    56\t\n    57\tShell profile setup is optional. Agent instructions can invoke project\n    58\tcommands directly through `.agents/bin/<command>` on Unix or\n    59\t`.agents\\bin\\<command>.cmd` on Windows. Global installation publishes\n    60\tforwarding shims to a safe existing user-bin directory when possible.\n    61\tSet `CURATOR_GLOBAL_USER_BIN` to a writable directory already on `PATH` when\n    62\tautomatic selection is unavailable.\n    63\t\n    64\tFor interactive bare command names, cache the hook once:\n    65\t\n    66\t```bash\n    67\tcurator shell-init --install\n    68\t# Add the source command printed above to .zshrc or .bashrc.\n    69\t```\n    70\t\n    71\tOn Windows, automatic detection selects PowerShell unless `SHELL` identifies\n    72\tGit Bash. Add the printed dot-source command to the PowerShell profile only if\n    73\tinteractive activation is wanted:\n    74\t\n    75\t```powershell\n    76\tcurator shell-init --install\n    77\t```\n    78\t\n    79\tThe cached hook is sourced without starting Curator on each shell launch.\n    80\t`CURATOR_AUTO_ENV=0` disables project-directory scanning while retaining\n    81\tglobal activation. Curator never edits a shell profile automatically.\n    82\t\n    83\t## CI example\n    84\t\n    85\tPin a released Curator version using the platform package or verified release\n    86\tartifact, then run the same protocol gates as local development:\n    87\t\n    88\t```yaml\n    89\tsteps:\n    90\t  - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    91\t  - name: Install Curator v0.1.1\n    92\t    run: go install github.com/relux-works/curator/cmd/curator@v0.1.1\n    93\t  - name: Materialize skills\n    94\t    run: curator install . --strict-tags\n    95\t  - name: Verify installed state\n    96\t    run: curator status . --check\n    97\t```\n    98\t\n    99\tOrganizations normally install enforced source, audit, and registry policy\n   100\tbefore this job. CI MUST NOT disable a policy required on developer machines.\n   101\t\n   102\t## External repository lifecycle\n   103\t\n   104\tSchema-7 external build repositories use\n   105\t[manager-profile section 11](../profiles/manager.md#11-external-repository-manager-profile).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
