{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"task-board resource get TASK-260720-1nvomm TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md --output - | nl -ba | sed -n '1511,1668p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1511\t  \"build_source\": {\n  1512\t    \"algorithm\": \"curator-build-source-v1\",\n  1513\t    \"content_sha256\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"\n  1514\t  },\n  1515\t  \"build_roots\": [\n  1516\t    \"build\"\n  1517\t  ],\n  1518\t  \"builds\": {\n  1519\t    \"local-helper\": {\n  1520\t      \"driver\": \"go-v1\",\n  1521\t      \"receipt_schema_version\": 1,\n  1522\t      \"cache_key\": \"sha256:1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111\",\n  1523\t      \"receipt_sha256\": \"sha256:2222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222\",\n  1524\t      \"artifact_sha256\": \"sha256:3333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333\",\n  1525\t      \"artifact_path\": \"bin/local-helper\"\n  1526\t    },\n  1527\t    \"golden-tool\": {\n  1528\t      \"driver\": \"go-repository-v1\",\n  1529\t      \"receipt_schema_version\": 2,\n  1530\t      \"repository\": \"golden-tools\",\n  1531\t      \"declared_identity\": {\n  1532\t        \"kind\": \"network-git\",\n  1533\t        \"value\": \"github.com/example/golden-tools\"\n  1534\t      },\n  1535\t      \"declared_locked_commit\": {\n  1536\t        \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n  1537\t        \"hex\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\"\n  1538\t      },\n  1539\t      \"declared_tag\": \"v1.4.0\",\n  1540\t      \"effective_identity\": {\n  1541\t        \"kind\": \"network-git\",\n  1542\t        \"value\": \"github.com/example/golden-tools\"\n  1543\t      },\n  1544\t      \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n  1545\t      \"commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n  1546\t      \"substituted\": false,\n  1547\t      \"build_source\": {\n  1548\t        \"algorithm\": \"curator-build-source-v1\",\n  1549\t        \"content_sha256\": \"sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\"\n  1550\t      },\n  1551\t      \"descriptor_target\": \"golden-tool\",\n  1552\t      \"cache_key\": \"sha256:4444444444444444444444444444444444444444444444444444444444444444\",\n  1553\t      \"receipt_sha256\": \"sha256:5555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555\",\n  1554\t      \"artifact_sha256\": \"sha256:6666666666666666666666666666666666666666666666666666666666666666\",\n  1555\t      \"artifact_path\": \"bin/golden-tool\"\n  1556\t    }\n  1557\t  }\n  1558\t}\n  1559\t```\n  1560\t\n  1561\tFor an unsubstituted external build, `declared_tag` may be written only from a\n  1562\treceipt whose producing operation completed the exact-tag/locked-commit check.\n  1563\tMarker parsing does not turn that field into independent provenance, and\n  1564\tread-only status does not contact the remote to re-test later tag movement.\n  1565\t\n  1566\t### 9.1 Snapshot and artifact keys\n  1567\t\n  1568\t- Protected external snapshot key: effective identity kind/value, effective object format, full effective commit, and external build-source digest.\n  1569\t- Artifact key: SHA-256 of the entire receipt input, including both declared and effective states, command key, descriptor target, build root/source directory, target, toolchain, and policy.\n  1570\t- Snapshot bytes may be deduplicated only when the complete snapshot key matches. Audit decisions remain subject-specific.\n  1571\t- Artifacts may be reused only when the complete receipt input and protected entry validate. Different declarations, substitutions, commands, targets, toolchains, or policy revisions do not alias.\n  1572\t- Physical object, snapshot, artifact, receipt, lock, and quarantine paths remain implementation-specific.\n  1573\t\n  1574\t### 9.2 Read-only status\n  1575\t\n  1576\tStatus MUST NOT fetch, repair, quarantine, alter permissions, refresh a snapshot, invoke a compiler, or execute an artifact.\n  1577\t\n  1578\tIt:\n  1579\t\n  1580\t1. derives the current effective plan from manifest and operator dev configuration;\n  1581\t2. validates marker v3 and substitution equality;\n  1582\t3. revalidates every referenced protected skill/external snapshot and artifact boundary;\n  1583\t4. recomputes available build-source identities, receipt inputs/keys, receipt hashes, and artifact relationships;\n  1584\t5. structurally validates manager-owned shims and PATH exposure.\n  1585\t\n  1586\tOutcomes:\n  1587\t\n  1588\t- an identity, commit, digest, target, receipt, artifact, shim, or substitution mismatch is non-current;\n  1589\t- an untrusted or corrupt snapshot/artifact boundary is non-current;\n  1590\t- a missing required snapshot is non-current when the marker claims it should exist;\n  1591\t- when existing profile semantics distinguish unavailable evidence from drift, a source that cannot be proved read-only may be reported `unknown`, but MUST NOT be reported current and `status --check` MUST return non-zero;\n  1592\t- status never contacts the remote merely to test availability or tag movement.\n  1593\t\n  1594\t### 9.3 Repair\n  1595\t\n  1596\tRepair resolves the current effective operator substitution if present, otherwise the declared locked source. It reacquires into operation-private state, repeats object proof, validation, identity, and audit, and rebuilds or reuses only after protected admission. It never adopts an untrusted snapshot or artifact by changing permissions.\n  1597\t\n  1598\tFor an unsubstituted declaration containing `tag`, repair always reacquires by\n  1599\tthe exact-tag-only flow and rechecks terminal equality with the immutable lock.\n  1600\tIt cannot use a successful direct-object fetch or an old protected snapshot as\n  1601\ta substitute for that operation's tag assertion.\n  1602\t\n  1603\tIf repair cannot obtain the exact source, it fails before installation mutation. Publication, marker/shim changes, rollback, and consumer update use the existing manager-home mutation lock and journal.\n  1604\t\n  1605\t### 9.4 Garbage collection roots\n  1606\t\n  1607\tGC revalidates cache boundaries and, under the manager-home mutation lock:\n  1608\t\n  1609\t- valid marker v3 files mark every referenced local skill raw snapshot, external frozen snapshot key, receipt/artifact key, and manager-generated shim relation;\n  1610\t- in-flight transaction journals mark every staged/published snapshot and artifact needed for commit or rollback;\n  1611\t- valid marker v1/v2 behavior remains unchanged;\n  1612\t- receipt content alone is never a live root;\n  1613\t- unreadable markers/journals or unprovable cache boundaries retain uncertain entries conservatively;\n  1614\t- GC never executes or adopts source or artifact bytes.\n  1615\t\n  1616\t## 10. Deterministic build, install, PATH, and rollback\n  1617\t\n  1618\t`go-repository-v1` reuses the accepted `go-v1` trusted Go session, environment, full dependency checks, directive/native-input rejection, fixed `go list`/`go build` vectors, internal-link policy, artifact checks, and no-execution rule. Its source acquisition and receipt semantics are distinct, so the driver ID is distinct.\n  1619\t\n  1620\tNormative order:\n  1621\t\n  1622\t1. Validate schema-7 manifest, URL/lock/tag grammar, substitutions, descriptor-independent collisions, and static local build-root exclusions.\n  1623\t2. Resolve every exact effective external commit into operation-private state;\n  1624\t   for each unsubstituted tagged declaration this means the sole exact-tag\n  1625\t   fetch and terminal-lock equality check, never a direct-object attempt.\n  1626\t3. Close the Git object boundary, freeze the whole snapshot, compute its digest, parse the descriptor, and validate target/module containment.\n  1627\t4. Audit consuming skill and every external repository independently.\n  1628\t5. Probe/fingerprint the trusted Go toolchain and derive all local receipt-v1 and external receipt-v2 inputs.\n  1629\t6. Inspect protected artifact candidates. On real misses, run fixed preflight/build into operation-private staging. Dry-run stops before source-aware Go commands as defined by the accepted driver policy.\n  1630\t7. Validate/hashes artifacts and generate canonical receipts/marker.\n  1631\t8. Under the home mutation lock, recover/revalidate, publish immutable snapshots/artifacts, and commit all targets with the consumer ledger last.\n  1632\t9. On failure, reverse rollback under the same lock. Pre-publication source/audit/build failures leave live state unchanged.\n  1633\t\n  1634\tPATH and shims are verified structurally:\n  1635\t\n  1636\t- command key passes existing portable/collision rules;\n  1637\t- shim is manager-owned and points exactly to the marker-selected protected artifact;\n  1638\t- artifact is one regular singly linked executable matching receipt path/hash;\n  1639\t- no shim points into a Git object database, frozen source snapshot, checkout, staging directory, or script runtime;\n  1640\t- environment exposure contains only the manager-generated bin directory;\n  1641\t- validation never calls a shell, `command -v`, or the built output.\n  1642\t\n  1643\tSeveral commands may select one logical descriptor target, but each manifest command key derives its own output and cache input. The repository still cannot request aliases, sidecars, post-build copies, or secondary PATH entries.\n  1644\t\n  1645\t## 11. Signing and notarization boundary\n  1646\t\n  1647\tSigning identities and notarization credentials are operator/platform secrets. They MUST NOT appear in a manifest, descriptor, repository, compiler environment, receipt trust field, or marker.\n  1648\t\n  1649\tThe first `go-repository-v1` release performs no manager post-signing. It does not invoke `codesign`, `signtool`, timestamping, or a notary service.\n  1650\t\n  1651\tA future local signer requires a separately reviewed profile/driver revision with:\n  1652\t\n  1653\t- operator-only opaque keychain/certificate/HSM/service identity;\n  1654\t- fixed signer executable, argv, entitlements/options, process graph, and network policy;\n  1655\t- signer policy/tool identity and signed bytes in cache/receipt identity;\n  1656\t- no package entitlements, certificate selector, timestamp URL, or arguments;\n  1657\t- private staging, no artifact execution, protected publication, and rollback.\n  1658\t\n  1659\tUntil standardized, a platform policy requiring local signing rejects source-built artifacts.\n  1660\t\n  1661\tApple Developer ID signing/notarization and Windows Authenticode/timestamping remain controlled release-pipeline work. A future prebuilt driver may verify signed release artifacts under its own exact digest and attestation policy; local build receipts do not become release provenance.\n  1662\t\n  1663\tLinux remains a separate later native-validation task. No Linux conformance claim is made until the same driver, sandbox/resource, shim, and lifecycle vectors pass natively.\n  1664\t\n  1665\t## 12. Future closed-driver rule\n  1666\t\n  1667\tThe external Git envelope may be shared, but compiler semantics are never generic. Every language adds a new driver ID and independent protocol/security review covering:\n  1668\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
