{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"task-board resource get TASK-260720-1nvomm TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md --output - | nl -ba | sed -n '1669,1732p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1669\t- complete compiler-visible inputs and dependency containment;\n  1670\t- trusted toolchain/sysroot/runtime identity;\n  1671\t- fixed process graph, environment, flags, target, output, and signer boundary;\n  1672\t- rejection of hooks, plugins, macros, generators, annotation processors, build tasks, recipes, response files, package linkers, and produced-program execution;\n  1673\t- offline dependency model and exact source identity;\n  1674\t- receipt/marker/cache identity, dry-run, audit-before-build, rollback/recovery, status/repair/GC, and platform vectors.\n  1675\t\n  1676\tConsequences remain:\n  1677\t\n  1678\t- Rust: Cargo `build.rs` and procedural macros are rejected; any direct `rustc` driver needs a closed dependency/link model.\n  1679\t- Swift: SwiftPM manifests/plugins/macros are rejected; direct `swiftc` must own SDK, target, graph, linker, and macro policy.\n  1680\t- Kotlin/JVM: Maven/Gradle, annotation processors, and compiler plugins are rejected; a direct driver owns class/module path, packaging, and JDK/Kotlin identity.\n  1681\t- C/C++: Make/CMake/Meson/Ninja are rejected; a direct driver owns sources, preprocessing, headers/sysroot, response files, compiler/linker plugins, native libraries, and output.\n  1682\t- .NET: MSBuild, analyzers, and source generators are rejected; a direct driver owns references, runtime packaging, native host, and signing.\n  1683\t\n  1684\tAdding an external repository does not make an unsafe build frontend safe.\n  1685\t\n  1686\t## 13. Threat model\n  1687\t\n  1688\t### 13.1 Adversary-controlled\n  1689\t\n  1690\t- consuming skill and manifest;\n  1691\t- declared Git URL, refs/tags served by the remote, object bytes, paths/modes, descriptor, source/vendor/embed inputs, sizes, diagnostics, and compiled artifact;\n  1692\t- source repository configuration and object-database indirection until rejected;\n  1693\t- candidate snapshot/receipt/marker/artifact cache bytes until protected admission;\n  1694\t- network failure, replay, moved tag, malicious remote, and compiler resource-exhaustion input.\n  1695\t\n  1696\t### 13.2 Trusted computing base\n  1697\t\n  1698\t- manager/protocol implementation;\n  1699\t- operator-selected Git distribution, HTTPS/SSH transport, credential and host-verification broker;\n  1700\t- operating system, filesystem containment, locks, protected caches, and transaction journal;\n  1701\t- operator-trusted Go toolchain and fingerprint;\n  1702\t- canonical JSON and hash implementations;\n  1703\t- any future separately standardized signer and opaque signing identity.\n  1704\t\n  1705\t### 13.3 Required controls\n  1706\t\n  1707\t| Threat | Control |\n  1708\t|---|---|\n  1709\t| Mutable/symbolic revision | Full object-format commit lock; optional safe tag must peel exactly |\n  1710\t| Declared/effective substitution confusion | Both states and substitution type in receipt-v2 input/cache key |\n  1711\t| Replace refs or grafts | Reject refs/grafts and use `--no-replace-objects` |\n  1712\t| Partial clone or lazy fetch | Reject promisor state and use `--no-lazy-fetch`; prove all tree/blob objects local |\n  1713\t| Alternates/object-store escape | Reject alternate files/env and manager-copy into private object DB |\n  1714\t| Fetch default or tag fallback widens state/process graph | Exact fresh-repo init/fetch argv; no-tag declarations use only the full lock, tagged declarations use only the exact tag ref; fixed destination; no auto-tags, branches, submodules, `FETCH_HEAD`, maintenance, commit graph, refmap, filter, or server option |\n  1715\t| Ambient config/URL rewrite/proxy/helper | Empty global/system config, manager-owned repo, fixed config/env/process graph |\n  1716\t| SSH MITM, system config, or variant argv | `GIT_SSH_VARIANT=ssh`; exact wrapper shape; `-F` empty config; operator-known hosts; fixed OpenSSH argv |\n  1717\t| Local repository extension/ref ambiguity | Admit only ordinary files-ref layout; byte-level config/ref parser; reject gitfile, commondir, bare, reftable, or unknown extensions |\n  1718\t| Malicious/incomplete pack metadata | Pack v2/v3 plus index-v2 admission, hash-family filenames/trailers, inert private copying, fixed trusted `cat-file --batch`, and manager object-ID recomputation |\n  1719\t| Object-reader transformation or process escape | One full-OID-only batch grammar; no `ls-tree`, revision/path input, filter, textconv, mailmap, alternate, lazy fetch, or object-reader child |\n  1720\t| Commit/tag parser disagreement | One ordered manager byte grammar, reserved-header uniqueness, exact separator, actual target-type checks, and one stable semantic error on both source paths |\n  1721\t| Hook/filter/LFS/submodule execution | Raw object extraction; no checkout/archive transforms; pinned Git LFS 3.7.1-family conservative all-blob detector; reject gitlinks |\n  1722\t| Package output/argv/signing selection | Strict descriptor; command-key output; closed driver; no signing fields |\n  1723\t| Audit bypass on cache hit | Exact snapshot validation/hash/audit before artifact-cache lookup |\n  1724\t| Forged cache | Protected boundary plus exact digests; rebuild rather than adopt |\n  1725\t| Shim/PATH hijack | Structural no-follow/hash validation; manager-generated shims; never execute output |\n  1726\t| Partial/cross-project install | One manager-home journaled transaction; consumer last; reverse rollback |\n  1727\t\n  1728\tSame-principal/admin compromise remains outside the local protected-cache invariant. Receipt and marker hashes are consistency/currentness identifiers, not signatures.\n  1729\t\n  1730\t## 14. Exact impact on existing board work\n  1731\t\n  1732\tThis scope is a n